STATEMENT OF CHANGES (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
----------------------------------------------
Files in this distribution have been modified from the upstream work. The
principal changes are:

  - Support for Canadian accounts, which the v3 cloud cannot serve at all: a new
    src/kumo-v2.ts signs in once to https://mesca-prod.kumocloud.com/login/v2 and
    reads the unit inventory, each unit's real capability profile, and the two
    secrets its WiFi adapter authenticates with. Selected by cloudRegion: "ca".
  - A v3 kill switch, so that mode contacts no v3 endpoint at any point: no
    login, no streaming, no zone polling, no cloud fallback for a command.
  - Config reconciliation (reconcileImpliedConfig): the Homebridge UI writes every
    schema default into config.json when the settings form is saved, which made a
    working install go idle over a contradiction the user never typed. Harmful
    schema defaults were removed for fields whose absence is meaningful.
  - Log redaction extended to the v2 sign-in and the v3 payload paths.
  - Setpoint quantization made account-aware: a Celsius account uses the 0.5 grid
    the Home app renders on, rather than the Fahrenheit-anchored grid.
  - Several concurrency fixes in the HomeKit write path, each found on real
    hardware and pinned by a regression test: a scene turning the unit on no
    longer loses its setpoints; a scene turning it off can no longer revive it
    through the Fanv2 tile; a superseded post-write reconcile no longer publishes
    a stale value; a redundant mode command is no longer sent.
  - An isolated device_authentication_error is treated as transient — retried
    once, and warned about only after three consecutive rejections. It is not the
    permanent configuration fault the code assumed: verified on real hardware.
  - Security hardening: every cloud call that carries a credential or token —
    the v3 login, refresh, authenticated-request and status paths, and the v2
    sign-in — refuses redirects (redirect: 'error'); a device address arriving
    from the cloud or from config must parse as an IPv4[:port] before it can
    become a signed request URL (isLocalHost, enforced at the single setCreds
    choke point); a local HTTP reply is capped at 64 KB and aborted mid-stream
    past that. SECURITY.md, new in this fork, states the threat model, the
    accepted residual risks, and the private reporting channel.
  - The package was renamed: this distribution is homebridge-mitsubishi-heatpump-ca,
    so it does not ship under the upstream npm name.

See CHANGELOG.md for the full list.

